Rule 3 (each dimension size of a tensor input is non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (input can be a tensor or a non-empty tuple of tensors)
{v_1 : tensor ⊎ tuple(tensor)} |= 0 ≤ ndim(v_1) ∨ v_1.len ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (valid index bounds for iterating over a tuple of tensors)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : i ≥ 0 ∧ i ≤ v_1.len - 1
>>
Rule 6 (non-empty tuple implies its largest valid index is non-negative)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= if v_1.len > 0 then v_1.len - 1 ≥ 0
